---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import EmailReveal from '../components/ui/EmailReveal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  num="§"
  label="Privacy"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles personal data and what this website stores in your browser.`}
>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>{site.name}</strong>, a team of college students in Thailand, decides how your personal
    data from this website is used (the "data controller" under Thailand's Personal Data Protection
    Act B.E. 2562, "PDPA"). We are staying anonymous for now. Contact us about your data here:
  </p>
  <p>
    <EmailReveal subject="Privacy request — larplabth.com" label="show privacy contact" />
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect, and why</h2>
  <div class="legal__scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Why</th>
          <th>Basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <strong>Contact form:</strong> name, email, company (optional), topic, your message
          </td>
          <td>To read your message and reply to it</td>
          <td>Your request / consent (you send it and accept this policy)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <strong>Your choices:</strong> that you accepted the Terms and this policy (with the
            version, language and time), and whether you want email updates
          </td>
          <td>To be able to show what you agreed to, and to respect your choice</td>
          <td>Legal obligation / consent</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <strong>Technical data</strong> (IP address, browser type) handled by Cloudflare
          </td>
          <td>To deliver the site, block bots and spam, and keep it secure</td>
          <td>Legitimate interest</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We don't have user accounts, don't sell personal data and don't run advertising or tracking
    cookies. We don't ask for sensitive data; please don't put any in your message.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Email updates</h2>
  <p>
    We send updates <strong>only if you tick the separate, optional box</strong> on the contact
    form. Unticked means no marketing email. You can withdraw at any time by writing to us; we will
    stop. Replying to your message is not marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who handles your data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site, runs the contact form's backend and the Turnstile
      bot check, and provides privacy-friendly visit counts without cookies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resend</strong> delivers the contact-form email to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google (Gmail)</strong> is where our team's inbox is kept.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers operate outside Thailand, so your data may be processed abroad under their own
    safeguards and policies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Messages that don't lead to a project: up to <strong>12 months</strong>, then deleted.
    </li>
    <li>If we work together: for as long as the work and our records need.</li>
    <li>Email-update opt-ins: until you withdraw.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="storage">6. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We don't use advertising or tracking cookies. This is everything the site can keep in your
    browser, and what it is for:
  </p>
  <div class="legal__scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
          <th>When it is saved</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>larp-consent</code>
          </td>
          <td>Remembers your choice on the storage notice so we don't ask every visit</td>
          <td>Essential — always, once you choose</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>theme</code>
          </td>
          <td>Remembers light or dark mode</td>
          <td>Only if you accept storage</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>larp-tetris-best</code>
          </td>
          <td>Remembers your best Tetris score</td>
          <td>Only if you accept storage</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare Turnstile</td>
          <td>
            Bot check, loaded only when you use the contact form; Cloudflare sets what it needs to
            run the check
          </td>
          <td>Security — only when you use the form</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Choosing "essential only" keeps the site fully working, it just won't save your theme or score,
    and removes them if they were saved. You can change your mind any time:
    <button type="button" class="legal__btn mono" data-open-consent>
      open storage settings
    </button>
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the PDPA you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>tell you what data we hold about you and give you a copy,</li>
    <li>correct it, or delete it,</li>
    <li>stop using it, or object to how it is used,</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time (this doesn't affect what we did before).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Write to us using the privacy contact above and we'll answer. If you're not happy, you can
    complain to Thailand's Personal Data Protection Committee.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy the version number above changes. The version you accepted is saved
    with your message.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>

<style>
  .legal__btn {
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line-strong);
    color: var(--c-text);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .legal__btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-text);
  }
</style>
